311
00:13:41,680 --> 00:13:44,540
The Art & Coffin is totes adorbs, so I'm chillin'.

312
00:13:44,540 --> 00:13:49,420
Hold up. Isn't your grandpa going to get worried if you don't make it home soon?

313
00:13:49,420 --> 00:13:51,160
It's fine. He's not at home right now, either.

314
00:13:51,160 --> 00:13:52,160
Huh?

315
00:13:52,160 --> 00:13:57,160
He stays over at my cousin's place on the weekends. They live near his chiropractor's office.

316
00:13:57,160 --> 00:14:01,160
After his appointment, he spends the night with them and then goes straight to the workshop the next day.

317
00:14:01,160 --> 00:14:03,160
You mean he's not working at home?

318
00:14:03,160 --> 00:14:05,900
Sometimes he does. But he's been busy at the workshop lately.

319
00:14:05,900 --> 00:14:08,900
So no one at home? I see.

320
00:14:08,900 --> 00:14:10,900
Does that mean you can stay over late?

321
00:14:10,900 --> 00:14:12,900
So approximately how long do I got with ya?

322
00:14:12,900 --> 00:14:14,900
I shouldn't stay out too late.

323
00:14:14,900 --> 00:14:16,900
You want to spend the night?

324
00:14:16,900 --> 00:14:18,900
Come again?

325
00:14:18,900 --> 00:14:20,900
You goober! That was a joke!

326
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:22,900
Yeah, of course.

327
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:25,260
Oh, you guess what I want.

328
00:14:51,260 --> 00:14:51,860
Woo-hoo.

329
00:14:51,860 --> 00:14:52,740
He's playing with the Pit Calvary Club.

330
00:14:52,740 --> 00:15:10,560
Hey, you're right. The art is adorable.

331
00:15:10,780 --> 00:15:13,020
It rules! Let me show you.

332
00:15:13,340 --> 00:15:15,060
